      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe and may be a typo.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the maximum for a single dose is about 1,000 mg. Doses this high greatly raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided as 850 mg PO twice daily.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting the intentional above-maximum dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
