       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your reason, getting things settled before the family visits and evening rounds, doesn't address the safety problem. At 5,100 mg/day, this dose carries a real risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, and nothing in the patient's profile offsets it. Entering it would be a knowing overdose.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals**, or another titration you prefer\n\nIf you think there's a clinical reason for a dose above the maximum, please talk with pharmacy or the clinical decision support team. They can review it and enter it through the hospital's override process, with documented rationale and monitoring.\n\nIf you give me a corrected dose, I'll enter it now."
